{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 210372, "name": "derzinn", "username": "derzinn", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/eb7434/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-17T19:46:16.843Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello. I just upgraded my Fedora workstation from 36 to 37. As usual, the upgrade process via  gnome-software ran smoothly and without any problems. Good work!</p>\n<p>I usually run <code>sudo dnf autoremove</code> from time to time, but this time I’m unsure:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">[zinn@zmac ~]$ sudo dnf autoremove\n[sudo] Passwort für zinn:         \nLetzte Prüfung auf abgelaufene Metadaten: vor 0:17:58 am Fr 17 Mär 2023 19:53:57 CET.\nAbhängigkeiten sind aufgelöst.\n==================================================================================================================================================================================\n Paket                                                     Architektur                      Version                                     Paketquelle                         Größe\n==================================================================================================================================================================================\nEntfernen:\n distribution-gpg-keys                                     noarch                           1.85-1.fc37                                 @updates                            539 k\n enchant                                                   x86_64                           1:1.6.0-31.fc37                             @fedora                             149 k\n f36-backgrounds-base                                      noarch                           36.1.1-2.fc37                               @fedora                             7.4 M\n f36-backgrounds-gnome                                     noarch                           36.1.1-2.fc37                               @fedora                             704  \n fedora-flathub-remote                                     noarch                           1-3.fc37                                    @fedora                             5.9 k\n fedora-third-party                                        noarch                           0.10-3.fc37                                 @fedora                              80 k\n fedora-workstation-repositories                           noarch                           35-4.fc37                                   @fedora                             3.4 k\n geocode-glib                                              x86_64                           3.26.4-1.fc37                               @fedora                             169 k\n gettext                                                   x86_64                           0.21.1-1.fc37                               @updates                            4.9 M\n gfbgraph                                                  x86_64                           0.2.5-2.fc37                                @fedora                             105 k\n gnome-online-miners                                       x86_64                           3.34.0-10.fc36                              @anaconda                           376 k\n info                                                      x86_64                           6.8-4.fc37                                  @fedora                             492 k\n libchamplain                                              x86_64                           0.12.20-7.fc37                              @fedora                             409 k\n libchamplain-gtk                                          x86_64                           0.12.20-7.fc37                              @fedora                              25 k\n libgweather                                               x86_64                           40.0-4.fc37                                 @fedora                              22 M\n libindicator-gtk3                                         x86_64                           12.10.1-23.fc37                             @fedora                             212 k\n mozjs91                                                   x86_64                           91.13.0-1.fc37                              @fedora                              12 M\n openldap-compat                                           x86_64                           2.6.4-1.fc37                                @updates                             59 k\n pcre-cpp                                                  x86_64                           8.45-1.fc37.2                               @fedora                              49 k\n pcre-devel                                                x86_64                           8.45-1.fc37.2                               @fedora                             1.7 M\n pcre-utf16                                                x86_64                           8.45-1.fc37.2                               @fedora                             483 k\n pcre-utf32                                                x86_64                           8.45-1.fc37.2                               @fedora                             463 k\n python3-click                                             noarch                           8.1.3-1.fc37                                @fedora                             1.1 M\n python3-libxml2                                           x86_64                           2.10.3-2.fc37                               @updates                            1.3 M\n\nTransaktionszusammenfassung\n==================================================================================================================================================================================\nEntfernen  24 Pakete\n\nFreigegebener Speicherplatz: 54 M\nIst dies in Ordnung? [J/n]: \n</code></pre>\n<p>A grep through the installed packages shows that <code>distribution-gpg-keys</code>, <code>libgweather</code> and <code>mozjs91</code> were replaced with other packages. Removing these packages should be safe.</p>\n<p>But I have no idea if <code>geocode-glib2</code> is a replacement for <code>geocode-glib</code>, for example.</p>\n<p>And what about <code>gettext</code> and <code>libindicator-gtk3</code> (a dependency of <code>gnome-shell-extension-appindicator</code>), those are definitely still needed, or am I wrong?</p>\n<p>What’s the general recommendation, just ignore it? Or should <code>dnf autoremove</code> generally not be executed?</p>\n<p>Thanks for your opinions.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T14:52:36.006Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 61, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 361.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79599, "topic_slug": "should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37", "display_username": "derzinn", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 13880, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37/79599/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [{"id": "fedora", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}, {"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 210389, "name": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "username": "vgaetera", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vgaetera/{size}/2552_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-17T23:50:19.809Z", "cooked": "<p>There’s a <a href=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/quick-docs/dnf-system-upgrade/#sect-clean-up-old-packages\">special warning</a> about removing presumably unused packages in the  official Fedora documentation for post-upgrade tasks.</p>\n<p>This should apply to most casual users to save time and avoid mistakes, but it might not be the best way to learn something new. <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-17T23:53:12.470Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 1, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 54.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79599, "topic_slug": "should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37", "display_username": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/quick-docs/dnf-system-upgrade/#sect-clean-up-old-packages", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "DNF System Upgrade :: Fedora Docs", "clicks": 20}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 13880, "username": "derzinn", "name": "derzinn", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/eb7434/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 549, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37/79599/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 3}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 210393, "name": "ilikelinux", "username": "ilikelinux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ilikelinux/{size}/27169_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-18T00:53:57.874Z", "cooked": "<p>Sometimes check the repolist also gives you some idea of packages you have installed from other sources then official.</p>\n<p><code>sudo dnf repolist</code></p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-18T00:53:57.874Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 9.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79599, "topic_slug": "should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37", "display_username": "ilikelinux", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Let's have a party (Fedora 44)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2081, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37/79599/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 210733, "name": "derzinn", "username": "derzinn", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/eb7434/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-03-20T09:23:38.017Z", "cooked": "<p>I checked the packages listed via</p>\n<p><code>dnf repoquery --installed --whatrequires gettext</code></p>\n<p>and was able to verify that these dependencies are no longer needed.</p>\n<p>So thank you for pointing me in the right direction. <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=12\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-20T09:23:38.017Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 17, "readers_count": 16, "score": 3.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 79599, "topic_slug": "should-i-run-dnf-autoremove-after-upgrade-from-f36-to-f37", "display_username": "derzinn", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 549, "username": "vgaetera", "name": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vgaetera/{size}/2552_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 13880, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wi